A||N||6||PocketRocket||Location Of Sending Unit?||||1||
Z||000000||PocketRocket||09-18-2000||07:04 PM||||Where is the sending unit for the Temperature Gauge on an 1985 V6 SE? I just bought my Fiero and I have no idea where everything is.  Thanks for the help.<P>------------------<BR>-Larry B<BR>'85 SE 2.8L||||reg||1
Z||000001||Phil||09-18-2000||10:04 PM||||Looking in from the trunk the gage/idiot light sensor is on the left in the head -should have 2 green or grn/wht wires. There 3 different temp sensors on the V6||||reg||1
Z||000002||PocketRocket||09-18-2000||10:34 PM||||Man that is hell to get too!<P>------------------<BR>-Larry B<BR>'85 SE 2.8L||||reg||11
Z||000003||StuGood||09-18-2000||11:41 PM||||No, it's not hard to get to at all.  Must be looking at the wrong sensor.  Let's try again...<P>Stand behind the car.  The temp. sending unit is on the lower, left rear corner of the aft (nearest) cylinder head.  It's pretty much right in front of you.<P>It's kind of stuck into the corner of the head, at an angle.  There's a two-pin connector on it, and a lot of times the plastic connector shell is crumbled away because of heat from the exhaust manifold.||||reg||5
Z||000004||PocketRocket||09-21-2000||04:32 PM||||I'm sorry, I still can't find it, you wouldn't happen to have a picture or know where one is do you?<P>------------------<BR>-Larry B<BR>'85 SE 2.8L<p>[This message has been edited by PocketRocket (edited 09-21-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||cobra427||09-21-2000||11:19 PM||||Ok pocketrock,let me give it a stab.As was said, stand in the back of the carlooking into the engine compartment.you will see the distributor on your left. The cylinders on the firewall side are 6,4,2<BR>              dist..&gt;O     +..w/pump<BR> cyls. on trunk side  5,3,1<BR>                     X<BR>X marks the spot where the sensor is located.<BR>There will be a small curved heat shield there that helps protect it from the exhaust manifold.<P>hope you find it <P>Jody||||reg||1
Z||000006||cobra427||09-21-2000||11:26 PM||||try this,<BR>................6,4,2,<BR>dis............O-----+--waterpump<BR>................5,3,1<BR>...............X<P>these things never come out like you want them to||||reg||1
